    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #221\n\n- 2026-09-19 03:33Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-19 05:05Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #442 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Branch `bb/relay-221-implementation-audit-fixes-21-23-decla-thr_c4mzd8tycr` pushed to origin. ## Summary Implements issue #221: declares task queue affinity (`\"api\"` vs `\"agents\"`) in module task descriptors and core task catalogs. - `@semprec/queue`: added `TASK_AFFINITIES`/`TaskAffinity`, `CORE_TASK_AFFINITY` map covering every `CORE_TASK_NAMES` entry, and `AGENT_TASK_NAMES` (`heartbeatFireAgent`, `agentRun`, `delegatedAgentRun`). - `@semprec/module-registry`: manifest schema now requires `queueAffinity: \"api\" | \"agents\"` on every module task descriptor, validated by Zod (fails load with an actionable error on missing/invalid values); `ModuleTaskProjection` carries it through. - `@semprec/data`: new `resolveTaskAffinitySets()` partitions core, agent, and module task names into `api`/`agents` sets and throws on any module/core-name collision; `ALL_MODULE_IDS` registry now reserves core/agent task names via `reservedTaskNames`. - Test fixtures and unit tests updated/added across `queue`, `module-registry`, and `data` packages to cover the new affinity data and validation failure paths. Verification: full `pnpm run verify` in `backend/` (lint, format, build, unit 45/45, import-path/migration/write-safety/boundary checks, integration 105/105, e2e 2/2) passed cleanly on a fresh run in this turn. No `web/` changes — this issue is backend-only. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-19 05:55Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #442 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed to `bb/relay-221-implementation-audit-fixes-21-23-decla-thr_c4mzd8tycr`. ## Summary Addressed the code-review findings on PR #442: - Added `DOC_HISTORY_SQUASH: \"docHistorySquash\"` to `CORE_TASK_NAMES`/`CORE_TASK_AFFINITY` (affinity `api`), the issue's exhaustive API handler set entry that was missing. - Added `docs/adr/2026-09-19-task-queue-affinity-routing.md` documenting the new `queueAffinity` cross-cutting pattern. - Left the `trashPurge` crontab findings unchanged — the issue's own Task and Acceptance criteria explicitly require that exact crontab line in this issue, and no composition root runs the worker against it yet (that's #91's scope), so it's inert declared data, not a live scheduling risk. The remote branch had a merge of `develop` pushed upstream since the last push; merged it in locally (clean, no conflicts — all my `trashPurge`/`docHistorySquash` changes intact) and re-ran the full `pnpm run verify` pipeline against the merged tree: unit 45/45, integration 112/112, e2e 2/2, no failures. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-19 06:05Z — This issue was resolved by #442, which just merged into develop.",
